<Base title="Sources, Methodology & Editorial Policy | HomeBackupCost" description="How HomeBackupCost picks sources and handles corrections." h1Name="Sources & editorial policy">
<h1>Sources, methodology &amp; editorial policy</h1>
<p class="lede">How we choose sources, date our numbers, label estimates, fix mistakes, and keep money out of our results.</p>
<h2>Where our numbers come from</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Primary sources first:</strong> manufacturer spec sheets and pricing pages, federal agencies (IRS, EIA, Ready.gov, CDC, CPSC, FDA, DOE), state energy offices, NASEO, and utilities.</li>
<li><strong>Established cost surveys</strong> such as EnergySage for installed battery and solar prices. When a number comes from a comparison site or contractor rather than the primary source, we say so.</li>
<li>The full source list and every calculator assumption are on the <a href="/about/#sources">About page</a>.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Editorial rules</h2>
<ul>
<li>Every figure links to its source and carries an "as of" date.</li>
<li>Estimates and assumptions are labeled <span class="badge est">Estimate</span>.</li>
<li>We do not publish invented statistics, reviews, testimonials, or activity counters. If we cannot verify a number, we leave it out and say so.</li>
<li>Safety guidance follows official agencies (Ready.gov, CDC, CPSC) and we always point readers to a licensed electrician for anything wired into a home.</li>
<li>We write in plain, calm language. No scare tactics.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Updates and corrections</h2>
<p>Each guide shows a "Last updated" date. Prices and program status change, so we re-check sources and update the date when we do. If you find an error, <a href="/contact/">tell us</a>; confirmed corrections are made on the page and the date is updated.</p>
<h2>Money and independence</h2>
<p>We may earn a commission from some product links or installer quote requests. That never changes a number or a ranking: calculator matches are sorted by fit and then price. See the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>
</Base>
